Promises -we use promises to handle asynchronous data 
Observables -we use Observables also to handle asynchronous data.

Differences 
When we need to use promises to handle asynchronous data ?

Promise -

1.A promise is native to javascript

2.Promise is eager.
It returns the data as soon as a promise is created.

3.Promise can emit only a single value.

4.Promise has methods for success and error.

5.Promise always returns asynchrnous data .

When we need to use promises to handle asynchronous data ?

Observable -

1.An observable is not native to javascript.
It is provided by a third party library called RXJS.

2.Observable is lazy.
It only emits the data if there is a subscriber for that observable.

3.Observables can emit single or multiple values.

4.Observables has methods for success,error and completion.

5.An observable can return both synchronous and asynchronous data based on
how it is implemented 
